# TAPD: Comment & Mention

Single-point write — generate one `tapd_comments_create` call per
invocation. Don't bundle multiple comments unless the user explicitly
asked (and even then, route through the bulk-cap rule HARD-RULE-5).

## Required fields

| field | default | from |
|---|---|---|
| `workspace_id` | per `tapd-overview` | cache |
| `entry_type` | — | user / context (`stories` / `bugs` / `tasks`) |
| `entry_id` | — | user (e.g. `1234`) |
| `description` | — | user message + @-translations applied |
| `author` | `$ME` | cache |

If the entity type is ambiguous, ask once: "评论到 story / bug / task 哪个？"

## @-mention translation

TAPD uses `[~user_name]` (literal characters) where `user_name` is the
**TAPD username**, not user id, not @id. So:

| User wrote | We send |
|---|---|
| `@张三` | `[~zhangsan]` (after lookup) |
| `@王五` | `[~wangwu]` |
| `@me` | `[~{{identity.tapdUserName}}]` |

### Username lookup

1. Read `~/.tapd/cache.json:knownUsers`. If the display name maps to a
   `tapd_user_id` and we have the corresponding `tapd_user_name`, use that.
2. If not in cache, call `tapd_users_list` once with a `name` filter (or
   list all and grep). The MCP server will append the result to
   `cache.json:knownUsers` automatically (see `mcp-skills` capability
   "knownUsers wiring" — note: this wiring is staged for a follow-up
   change, so for now you may need to write the user name yourself or
   re-call `tapd_users_list` next time).
3. If `users_list` doesn't return a match, **stop and ask** the user for
   the precise TAPD username:

   > 我在当前 workspace 找不到名为「张三」的用户。请告诉我他在 TAPD 里的
   > 精确登录名（不是显示名）：

   Don't guess; a wrong @ silently fails (TAPD just renders the literal
   text without notifying anyone).

## HTML 格式要求（必须遵守）

TAPD 评论的 `description` 字段**必须使用 HTML 格式**，不接受纯文本或 Markdown。
在发送任何评论之前，将用户提供的内容转换为合法的 HTML：

| 用户内容 | 转换为 HTML |
|---|---|
| 普通文本（无换行） | `<p>文本</p>` |
| 多段落 / 换行 | 每段用 `<p>...</p>` 包裹 |
| `**粗体**` | `<b>粗体</b>` |
| `*斜体*` | `<i>斜体</i>` |
| `` `代码` `` | `<code>代码</code>` |
| 代码块 ` ```...``` ` | `<pre><code>...</code></pre>` |
| 无序列表 `- item` | `<ul><li>item</li></ul>` |
| 有序列表 `1. item` | `<ol><li>item</li></ol>` |
| 链接 `[text](url)` | `<a href="url">text</a>` |
| `@mention` | `[~user_name]`（保持 TAPD mention 格式，不转换为 HTML） |

**示例**：用户说"请确认一下，`foo()` 返回值有问题"，发送：

```html
<p>请确认一下，<code>foo()</code> 返回值有问题</p>
```

## Send immediately, report after

Comments don't need a preview block. Just call the tool, then:

```
✓ 评论已发到 bug #1234 (comment id: 9999)
  @ 通知到: 张三 (zhangsan)
```

## Edge cases

- **Empty description** → refuse, ask the user what to say.
- **Description contains markdown** → 自动转换为 HTML（见上方 HTML 格式要求），无需询问用户。
- **User says "delete the comment"** → not supported (HARD-RULE-1). Tell
  user: "评论一旦发出，我无法删除。请在 TAPD 网页端手动删除/编辑。"
- **Multiple targets in one message** ("给 #1234 和 #5678 都评论") → split
  into separate calls; HARD-RULE-5 applies (cap 10), HARD-RULE-4
  exception applies (still no preview), but **before** sending, summarize
  all targets to the user once and ask "确认这 N 条评论都发？" — this is
  not a "preview" per HARD-RULE-4, it's a courtesy heads-up for batch.

## What this skill does NOT do

- Not a state changer (don't update status / owner from here — those are
  separate flows with preview).
- Not a markdown renderer (TAPD does HTML only).
- Not a comment editor (TAPD API typically doesn't support edit; ignore
  user requests for that).

## Tools used

- `tapd_comments_create` (the main call)
- `tapd_users_list` (for @-mention name lookup, when not in
  `knownUsers` cache)
